    World


Other common escape sequences:

    \n      Newline
    \t      Horizontal tab
    \\      Backslash
    \"      Double quote
    \'      Single quote
    \0      Null character


======================================================================
1.31 return 0;
======================================================================

Code:

    return 0;


This terminates main() and returns the value 0
to the operating environment.

Convention:

    0
      →
    successful termination


Non-zero values are commonly used to indicate
some kind of failure or special status.


======================================================================
1.32 SEMICOLON ;
======================================================================

Example:

    printf("Hello");

The semicolon generally terminates a C statement.

Example:

    int age = 25;

