======================================================================
1.33 COMMENTS
======================================================================

Comments are notes written for programmers.

The compiler does not treat normal comments as executable
program instructions.


Single-line comment:

    // This is a comment


Multi-line comment:

    /*
       This is
       a multi-line comment
    */


Example:

    #include <stdio.h>

    int main(void)
    {
        // Print message
        printf("Hello\n");

        return 0;
    }


======================================================================
1.34 BASIC STRUCTURE OF A C PROGRAM
======================================================================

General structure:

    #include <header.h>

    global declarations

    return_type function_name(parameters)
    {
        declarations;

        statements;

        return value;
    }


Simple example:

    #include <stdio.h>

    int main(void)
    {
        int a = 10;
        int b = 20;

        int sum = a + b;

        printf("Sum = %d\n", sum);

        return 0;
    }


Program flow:

    Start
      ↓
    main()
      ↓
    a = 10
      ↓
    b = 20
      ↓
    sum = a + b
      ↓
    printf()
      ↓
    return 0
      ↓
    End


