======================================================================
1.44 ERRORS IN PROGRAMMING
======================================================================

There are several important types of errors.


1. SYNTAX ERROR

    Code violates language syntax.

Example:

    int main(void)
    {
        printf("Hello")
        return 0;
    }

    Missing semicolon after printf().


2. COMPILATION ERROR

    The compiler cannot successfully translate the program.

    Causes may include:
        • Syntax errors
        • Invalid declarations
        • Type-related errors
        • Missing declarations


3. LINKER ERROR

    Compilation may succeed, but required symbols
    cannot be resolved during linking.

Example concept:

    Calling a function whose required definition/library
    is unavailable.


4. RUNTIME ERROR

    Error occurs while program is running.

Examples:

    • Invalid memory access
    • Division by zero in applicable situations
    • File operation failure


5. LOGICAL ERROR

    Program runs but produces the wrong result.

Example:

    Expected:
        10 + 20 = 30

    Programmer accidentally writes logic that performs:

        10 - 20 = -10


